# Overview
hs-sensor-shield module for netconfd (yuma123): Raspberry Pi implementation of
the hs-sensor-shield YANG module for the Heimonen Solutions sensor shield.

/sensor-shield reports:

 container              sensor    bus             values
 host                   -         device tree     serial-num, model
 particulate-matter     PMS7003   UART 9600 8N1   pm1-0, pm2-5, pm10 (ug/m3)
 carbon-dioxide         SCD41     I2C 0x62        co2 (ppm)
 air-quality            SGP41     I2C 0x59        voc-index, nox-index (1-500),
                                                  voc-raw, nox-raw
 temperature-humidity   SHT41     I2C 0x44        temperature (C), humidity (%RH)
 pressure               LPS22HB   I2C 0x5c/0x5d   pressure (hPa), temperature (C)
 illuminance            BH1750    I2C 0x23/0x5c   illuminance (lx)

Every sensor container carries <sensor> (part number), <oper-status> (ok or
unavailable) and, when ok, <last-update>.

The sensors are sampled continuously by the module:

 * an I2C thread samples the SHT41, SGP41, SCD41, LPS22HB and BH1750 once per
   second. The SGP41 raw signals are converted to VOC/NOx indices with the
   Sensirion gas index algorithm (which requires 1 Hz sampling; the baseline
   adapts over ~24 h, the index is 0 for the first 45 s and the NOx hotplate is
   conditioned for the first 10 s). The SHT41 reading compensates the SGP41 (the SCD41's own temperature and
   humidity are used when there is no SHT41).
   The SCD41 runs in periodic mode (a sample every 5 s).
 * a UART thread reads the PMS7003 frames.

A <get> returns the latest readings. A sensor whose last good reading is older
than 5 s (15 s for the SCD41, 10 s for the PMS7003) or that was never found is
reported with <oper-status>unavailable</oper-status> and no values. Sensors
that are not found are probed again every 10 s.

# Wiring
 I2C sensors: SDA -> GPIO 2, SCL -> GPIO 3 (i2c1, 100 kHz default)
 PMS7003:     TX  -> GPIO 15 (RXD, /dev/serial0), 5V, GND

The LPS22HB address depends on its SA0 pin and the BH1750 address on its ADDR
pin; both alternatives are probed (the LPS22HB is identified by WHO_AM_I first,
the BH1750 takes the other address).

# Raspberry Pi configuration
With raspi-config (Interface Options): enable I2C, enable the serial port
hardware and disable the login shell over serial. Non-interactively:

 sudo raspi-config nonint do_i2c 0
 sudo raspi-config nonint do_serial_hw 0
 sudo raspi-config nonint do_serial_cons 1
 sudo reboot

which results in /boot/firmware/config.txt containing
 dtparam=i2c_arm=on
 enable_uart=1
and no console=serial0,... in /boot/firmware/cmdline.txt.

The BH1750 DVI (reset / I2C reference) pin is wired to GPIO23 on the shield and
must be driven high, add to /boot/firmware/config.txt:
 gpio=23=op,dh

Note that the SGP41 (0x59) does not show up in i2cdetect (it NACKs the empty
probe) although it works; the expected scan shows 23, 44, 5c and 62.

Check with: sudo i2cdetect -y 1 (apt-get install i2c-tools)

The serial device can be overridden with the PMS7003_DEVICE environment variable.

# Dependencies
Installed netconfd and yangcli
 apt-get install netconfd yangcli libyuma-dev

# Installation
 autoreconf -i -f
 ./configure CFLAGS="-g -O0"  CXXFLAGS="-g -O0" --prefix=/usr
 make
 make install

The YANG module is installed to /usr/share/yuma/modules/hs-sensor-shield/.

# Testing installation

 netconfd --module=hs-sensor-shield --no-startup --superuser=$USER

Other terminal:
 yangcli --server=localhost --user=$USER

yangcli pi@localhost> xget /sensor-shield
...
  data {
    sensor-shield {
      host {
        serial-num 000000008c18491c
        model 'Raspberry Pi 4 Model B Rev 1.4'
      }
      particulate-matter {
        sensor PMS7003
        oper-status ok
        last-update 2026-08-28T12:00:01Z
        pm1-0 3
        pm2-5 5
        pm10 6
      }
      carbon-dioxide {
        sensor SCD41
        oper-status ok
        last-update 2026-08-28T12:00:00Z
        co2 612
      }
      air-quality {
        sensor SGP41
        oper-status ok
        last-update 2026-08-28T12:00:01Z
        voc-index 103
        nox-index 1
        voc-raw 30105
        nox-raw 15899
      }
      temperature-humidity {
        sensor SHT41
        oper-status ok
